  "scope": "Selected dependencies of finite two-process task decidability, and IIS graph characterization.",
  "adaptations": {
    "Model.lean": "Compatibility aliases for canonical DecisionTasks.Model Event, Task, Protocol, run, Solves, Obl, and silentEvent; no duplicate operational semantics. Generic lookup and source process spellings are retained.",
    "Views.lean": "Combined view bisimulation, reception separation, and full histories. Replaced leaderAlg and Determines with historyAlg, which only records history.",
    "NodeTransport.lean": "Added the three word-prefix definitions from Mso; made segLetters reduction explicit.",
    "TaskColouring.lean": "Combined the task characterization with taskColouring_annotated_form from Decision; used historyAlg instead of a leader algorithm. Protocol runs now use the shared dependent task model through transparent compatibility aliases.",
    "Colouring.lean": "Made the reception-bit reduction explicit after removing unused simp lemmas.",
    "Union.lean": "Replaced the independent IAR algorithm with aliases and notation lemmas over PriorityPairMonitor, a finite streaming adapter to the existing EncodedParityFamilies compiler. The task monitor now uses the compiler initial state and computed priority bound; branch_condition_iff is unchanged.",
    "Parity.lean": "Removed the duplicate finite game and tree-automaton development. Retained priority notation with a proved equivalence to NatSeqMinEvenParity and aliases of shared tree syntax. The executable generic RunTreeNonemptiness adapter calls existing TreeNonemptiness and FiniteOrbitParity.",
    "ColAut.lean": "Constructs the existing RunParityTreeAutomaton directly, with decidable transition relation; nonemptiness and regular-run witnesses use the shared library endpoints. Parity records use the existing compiler through PriorityPairMonitor; no independent parity-combination algorithm remains.",
    "Back.lean": "Acceptance proofs use shared run-tree transitions and min-even parity; task-specific branch and labelling obligations are unchanged."
  }
}
